# Review: VideoPlugin

The data model, both operations and the article layout are built. `Video` (in `@dxos/types`) carries
`transcript` and `summary` refs, `Transcribe` calls the EDGE `/transcription/video` endpoint and links a
new `Text`, and `Summarize` runs `AiRequest` with a Sonnet model and links a summary. The article
composes player, transcript and summary as separate surfaces with a tab strip and a regenerate action.
The interaction model diverged from the spec: transcription and summarization run automatically when
a surface opens (plus app-graph menu actions), not from a Transcribe/Summarize button; the summary
editor is editable, not read-only; the tab does not switch to Summary on completion. Tests cover only
pure helpers (embed URL parsing, YouTube utils, `Video.make`); no operation has a test.

Of 28 items: 4 done, 8 untested, 7 partial, 3 diverged, 6 missing. Findings:

- **No operation test.** `transcribeVideo` and `summarizeVideo` (T-3, T-4) have no test against a
  stubbed endpoint or AI service.
- **Triggers are automatic.** F-3.1, F-3.4 and F-4.1 describe user-triggered actions; the code
  auto-runs from `TranscriptSection` / `SummarySection` effects.
- **F-5.3 is missing.** Nothing switches the tab to Summary when summarization completes.

